    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1986-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have \\(\\sqrt[6]{27}=(3^3)^{\\frac{1}{6}}=\\sqrt3\\) and \\[ \\sqrt{6\\frac34}=\\sqrt{\\frac{27}{4}}=\\frac{3\\sqrt3}{2}. \\] Hence the expression is \\[ \\begin{aligned} \\left(\\sqrt3-\\frac{3\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)^2 &=\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)^2\\\\ &=\\frac34. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nThus the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite \\(27\\) as a power of \\(3\\) and \\(6\\frac34\\) as an improper fraction",
        "Simplify both radicals before squaring their difference"
      ],
